  description="Sorting 6,300+ known planets into families by size, orbit, and density — hot Jupiters, super-Earths, ocean and lava worlds — then two case studies up close: the Saturn system and the living machine of Earth."
  activeId="4.2" chapter={4} current="/chapter/4/4.2">
  <Hero
    tease="More than six thousand planets are now known, and almost none resemble home. Sort them by size and orbit and clean families appear — hot Jupiters, super-Earths, lava worlds, rare Earth-likes — while density betrays what each is made of. Then two case studies up close: Saturn, a miniature solar system of rings and shepherd moons, and Earth, whose churning core, layered air, and magnetic shield keep it alive."
